        (bold yes))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid "9c096aa1-b65f-56e8-968a-63ce2f8daf0c"))
  (text "NOTES\n1. Every header pin is labelled beside it on the front silkscreen (A9 = PA9); the back has a function cheat sheet.\n2. CAN (PB8 RX / PB9 TX, remapped) is logic level only: it needs an external CAN transceiver.\n3. USB and CAN cannot run at the same time on the STM32F103 (they share the packet RAM).\n4. The 3V3 header pins are outputs of the on-board LDO (U2); do not back-drive them from another supply.\n5. 5V pin = VSYS via PTC F1 + P-FET Q1: 5 V out on USB, or 4.5-5.5 V in (reverse-protected, no OVP)."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20.32 205.74 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.524 1.524))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid "d8951000-f706-5cc0-90b8-370c525f0d44"))
